ei example where it's applied to GigabitEthernet interfaces), the Juniper equivalent would be:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 synchronization\\nset interfaces ge-2/0/0 synchronization\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact Juniper syntax may vary slightly depending on the platform (MX, PTX, etc.) and Junos version. The above translation assumes a generic Junos implementation with synchronization support.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-2/0/0 synchronization'}]]": 1,
